# SFT execution status v0.127: raw-text-free failure-stage transport prepared

2026-09-27. The diagnostic blind spot is repaired in a versioned successor.
**264 local tests passed, with zero failures, errors or skips; Ruff passed.**
This is local preparation, not a native import pass or a root-cause fix for
the v0.126 failure. Gate 5 remains incomplete. No AWS command, new instance,
GPU, real model data, inference or training was used in this step.

## Narrow change

The frozen v1 worker discarded child stderr and collapsed all failures to a
generic result. New v2 entry/worker/launcher/supervisor files transport a
fixed allowlisted stage through process exit status and systemd observation.
Child stdout/stderr remain DEVNULL; no exception string, traceback, source,
candidate text or dynamic file path is collected. No additional log files
are produced by the worker. These codes locate the failing boundary; they
do not necessarily identify its internal cause.

Entry codes 40–50 distinguish single-use check, cold loader, runtime gate,
read-only inputs, writable output, control read, control contract, coordinator
import, result contract, independent checksum consumer and summary write.
Worker codes 60–66 distinguish worker boundary, worker arguments, preparation
source copy, import read-only binds, child dispatch, unknown child failure
and worker control load. Unknown child statuses are not trusted as stages.

The parent accepts a diagnostic code only with the corresponding failed,
normal-exit systemd state. Signals, OOM and timeout results cannot be interpreted
as a successful stage diagnosis. All failures still fail closed and stop the
exact unit. The existing exclusive attempt marker and empty-cgroup cleanup
rules remain. The new unit prefix and /opt release root use v2.

No parser, vocabulary, rights, checksum, resource, runtime-admission or
production gate was relaxed. Existing CPU/memory/tasks/time/tmpfs constraints,
private networking, private devices and source/input read-only bind properties
are unchanged. Old v1 files, bundle v0.2 and failed native evidence are preserved.

## Verification

- 32 diagnostic/successor tests plus 232 existing regression/bootstrap tests
  passed in 5.486 seconds using the existing local CPython 3.13.7 environment.
- Successor tests include actual tiny generated conversion/package/checksum
  flow, with Linux host observations substituted locally; no full-size model.
  Native systemd/mount/UID operations are doubled. Local success cannot prove
  Linux namespace behavior, actual 3.12 admission or future native success.
- Fixed-code transport, exception-string non-disclosure, child output discard,
  all diagnostic terminal statuses, cleanup and consumed-attempt rejection
  have synthetic coverage. OS properties match the predecessor exactly.
- The final parent audit hook recorded zero network and blocked-real-artifact
  attempts. This is not OS sandbox proof and does not automatically propagate
  to fresh test interpreters. Source-only archive verification is separate.
- Initial development invocations exposed a missing PYTHONPATH in the test
  command and an overbroad guard matching synthetic temporary /work subpaths;
  corrected test invocation/prefix matching before the final passing suite.
  No failed native attempt was rerun. Formatting findings were also corrected.
- All 49 files in the new archive match both its manifest and workspace
  sources; 51 members and the unchanged runtime-lock hash were verified.
  The staging successor's archive/manifest pins match. Staging was not run.

